# Line endings — added 2026-09-01.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Both repos already store every text file as LF in git
# (core.autocrlf=true converts on checkout), so the COMMITTED content has never
# diverged. The working tree is another matter: tools here write different
# endings, so at the time of writing brain-frontend held 65 CRLF files next to
# 85 LF ones, and secretarIA-frontend 37 next to 92. Nothing is broken by that
# on its own — but it makes a cross-repo `diff` of the same file report EVERY
# line as changed, because a plain diff treats the trailing \r as content.
#
# That is not hypothetical. The 2026-08-30 frontend audit compared
# lib/secretaria-hub.ts across the two repos, hit exactly this, and reported a
# "1739-line divergence" that was really 792 + 947 — the two files' whole
# lengths added together, i.e. "delete all of A, add all of B". The real
# divergence was a couple hundred lines. A finding was escalated on a number
# that measured the encoding, not the code.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` pins the working tree to LF regardless of core.autocrlf,
# so the next such comparison measures the code.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
